        "title": "Requirements Engineering and Management",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Requirements engineering (RE) defines what a system must do and the constraints it must satisfy. It is the highest-leverage SE activity — errors found in requirements are 100× cheaper to fix than errors found after deployment. It is also where most systems fail: not because of bad engineering, but because the wrong thing was built."
